  "body": "When a dialog closes without a previously focused element, its current focus can remain inside the closed dialog until the asynchronous focus fixup runs. Focus the document's viewport synchronously if focus is still inside the dialog; leave focus elsewhere alone.\n\nFixes #13118.\n\n- [ ] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed).\n- [ ] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at: [Chromium CL 8644932](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8644932) (WPT test in the Chromium checkout; not yet upstream).\n- [ ] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chromium: [41284677](https://issues.chromium.org/issues/41284677); [implementation CL](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8644932).\n   * Gecko: not filed.\n   * WebKit: not filed.\n- [ ] Corresponding [HTML AAM](https://w3c.github.io/html-aam/) & [ARIA in HTML](https://w3c.github.io/html-aria/) issues & PRs: not applicable; no accessibility mappings change.\n- [ ] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed: not filed.\n- [x] The commit has a clear commit message.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13119/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Oct 24, 2026, 7:34 AM UTC (e04355a)\">/acknowledgements.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13119/b342939...e04355a/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"